<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $89.1 mln May 14.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $89.1 mln May 14.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $89.1 million surplus on May 14 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MAY 14</p>
<p>Exports: $380.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $264.3 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $239.3 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $266.3 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $89.1 million</p>
<p>MAY DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.300 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.189 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.300 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.322 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.089 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
